<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>

<handout xml:id="pp-3">
    <title>Portfolio Problem 3</title>

    <paragraphs>
        <title>The Conjectures</title>

        <p>
            For this portfolio problem, you'll prove OR disprove BOTH of the
            following conjectures.
            Recall <q>conjecture</q> is a statement that is believed to be true
            but has not yet been proven.
            So it could be true or false.
            Start by trying some concrete example for each conjecture.
            You should include these examples in your handwritten draft and in
            your writing revision.
        </p>

        <conjecture>
            <statement>
                <p>
                    The sum of the cubes of any three consecutive integers is
                    divisible by 3.
                </p>
            </statement>
        </conjecture>

        <conjecture>
            <statement>
                <p>
                    The sum of the cubes of any three consecutive integers is
                    divisible by 4.
                </p>
            </statement>
        </conjecture>

        <p>
            After doing some examples, if you think the theorem is true, you
            should write it as a theorem and then write a proof of it.
            Your proof should start by <q>mathematizing</q> the theorem
            statement.
            (By that I mean, how do you turn <q>3 consecutive integers</q> into
            something you can work with?)
        </p>

        <p>
            If you believe a conjecture is false, say so and include one concrete
            counterexample.
            Use specific numbers and explain how they make the hypothesis true,
            but the conclusion is false.
            (You do not need to correct the theorem, just provide one
            counterexample!)
        </p>

        <p>
            A suggesting ordering for your written revision, is 
            <ol>
                <li>
                    <p>
                        First conjecture statement.
                    </p>
                </li>
                <li>
                    <p>
                        Examples related to the first conjecture.
                    </p>
                </li>

                <li>
                    <p>
                        Either write a theorem statement and a proof, or explain a counterexample.
                    </p>
                </li>

                <li>
                    <p>
                        Second conjecture statement.
                    </p>
                </li>

                <li>
                    <p>
                        Examples related to the second conjecture.
                    </p>
                </li>

                 <li>
                    <p>
                        Either write a theorem statement and a proof, or explain a counterexample.
                    </p>
                </li>
            </ol>
        </p>
    </paragraphs>
</handout>